## Summary

Continue Matrix `SURF-008` / ledger `PHIL-SURFACE-ELAB-001` by folding the exact context-free refinement bridge from #516 and binder-scoped refinement bridge from #517 into the existing intrinsic and binding-aware Grammar-v1 type dispatchers.

### Contract

- `grammarV1IntrinsicType` now delegates primitive-base context-free refinements only to the verified #516 bridge;
- `grammarV1BoundType` delegates every refinement type to the verified #517 temporary-binder bridge, so binder-dependent and context-free refinements share one binding-aware entry point without fallback reinterpretation;
- intrinsic primitive/Bytes/Proof/Frame/Validated/named routing remains unchanged;
- binding-aware Bytes and Proof routing remains unchanged;
- an active same-name outer binding still rejects rather than being shadowed by a refinement binder;
- UInt/Nat literal coercion remains unresolved and fail-closed, as do arithmetic/projection/specialization, nonprimitive refinement bases, tuple/product mode synthesis, and all other unresolved contextual forms;
- no general type→mode rule, evidence, coercion, alias resolution, specialization, or fallback type interpretation is invented.

### Executable pressure

The existing `Phase1GrammarV1IntrinsicTypeCompositionMain.hs` audit gate now requires refinement behavior through the normal dispatcher APIs: context-free refinement preservation, binder-scoped Bool relation/claim structure, compatible outer-reference use, active-name shadow rejection, and coercion-dependent rejection. No duplicate workflow step is added.

